WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.810
Before the parents' evening, I

2
00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:05.370
need every pupil in Six A with a

3
00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.730
maths mark under ten.

4
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.840
Our school has four hundred

5
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.860
pupils in one big sheet.

6
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:14.410
Scrolling?

7
00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:16.790
No thanks.

8
00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.570
Today: asking the database questions

9
00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.750
with SELECT, WHERE and ORDER BY.

10
00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.590
Every question starts the same way.

11
00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:30.690
SELECT says which columns you want back.

12
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.420
FROM says which table to look in.

13
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:35.990
And a star means every column.

14
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:38.940
WHERE picks the rows.

15
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.620
Equals, greater than, less than: class

16
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:47.020
equals six A, mark less than ten.

17
00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.890
Text goes in single quotes, and

18
00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:51.190
it must match exactly.

19
00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:54.000
AND needs both to be true;

20
00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.300
OR needs either one.

21
00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.160
ORDER BY sorts the answer.

22
00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.340
Add DESC for the biggest first.

23
00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.620
And LIMIT keeps only the first few

24
00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:07.880
rows: the top three, say.

25
00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:12.130
That's a query: a question in SQL.

26
00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:14.570
It describes the rows you

27
00:01:14.570 --> 00:01:16.510
want, not how to find them.

28
00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:19.110
The same query works on twelve

29
00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:20.570
rows or twelve million.

30
00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:22.330
Quick check!

31
00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:24.850
Which part of a query picks

32
00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.230
which rows come back?

33
00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:28.850
WHERE picks the rows;

34
00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:30.730
SELECT picks the columns.

35
00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.000
Keep them apart in your head:

36
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.620
columns across, rows down.

37
00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:38.370
Always check an answer

38
00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:39.630
against what you know.

39
00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.910
If WHERE class equals six A

40
00:01:42.910 --> 00:01:45.270
returns nobody, look at the data:

41
00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:48.210
maybe it says six small a.

42
00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.740
If a query returns half the

43
00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:52.780
school, a condition is missing.

44
00:01:54.070 --> 00:01:56.790
In the app, real SQL runs on your phone,

45
00:01:57.090 --> 00:01:58.730
on a school's pupils and marks.

46
00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.230
Pick a question, change it, and run it.

47
00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.000
Try changing five B to six

48
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.720
A, or AVG to MAX.

49
00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:09.860
Your turn.

50
00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.200
I want the three highest maths

51
00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.220
marks, biggest first.

52
00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:17.520
Which lines do that?

53
00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:22.230
ORDER BY mark DESC, then LIMIT three.

54
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.620
Remember: SELECT picks columns,

55
00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.340
FROM the table, WHERE the rows.

56
00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:31.450
Text goes in single

57
00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:33.170
quotes, matched exactly.

58
00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.940
And check every answer against

59
00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.260
what you already know.

60
00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:40.100
Try it in class tomorrow:

61
00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.800
play “Human database”.

62
00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:46.230
Each pupil holds a card with their class,

63
00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:49.650
birth month and how they travel.

64
00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:53.660
Read out a query: select pupils where

65
00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:57.800
travel is walking, order by birth month.

66
00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:01.220
The pupils who match step

67
00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.900
forward and line up in order.
